($q$B$q$,$q$ec218044-fa22-45a3-9371-7fce48c108e8$q$::uuid,$q$A1$q$,$q$The median is 22 minutes since it's the middle value when the data is ordered. The distribution is right-skewed because there's that one high value at 41 which is a potential outlier. When I calculate the mean I get (18+19+20+21+22+23+24+25+41)/9 = 213/9 which is about 23.7 minutes, so the mean is greater than the median. If we removed the 41 the mean would go down since we're taking out a really high value, and the standard deviation would also decrease because there would be less spread in the data.$q$,$q$anthropic$q$,$q${"content_key":"APSTATS-SFRQ-001","answer_type":"A1","expected":[{"criterion_key":"a1","present":true},{"criterion_key":"b1","present":true},{"criterion_key":"c1","present":true},{"criterion_key":"d1","present":true}]}$q$::jsonb,$q$fdd12be54bf9c0ab74d2f25eb89db878aa529cf3f709e914a467457947776e53$q$,$q$provisional_accept$q$,$q$99ffea1ddbf2afa69ad769a9ed32fac92f54df845a9cf90d91a4f2161e07a692$q$),
